// The scan target for the scanner-drift workflow, which copies this file to go.mod in a scratch directory and scans that with the latest Trivy and Grype. It is kept under another name so GitHub's dependency graph and Dependabot do not raise alerts for it: the module is never built, and its dependencies are vulnerable on purpose.
//
// The versions are pinned below several well-known Go advisories (GHSA / GO-…), so the target keeps producing findings even if one advisory is withdrawn or merged. Language advisories are not dropped when something reaches end of life, as a distribution's are, but they can be withdrawn. Replace a dependency only when a drift run reports that this target yielded no advisories at all.
module example.com/scanner-drift-target

go 1.20

require (
	golang.org/x/net v0.7.0
	golang.org/x/text v0.3.7
	gopkg.in/yaml.v3 v3.0.0-20210107192922-496545a6307b
)
